#!/bin/bash\n\n# 🚀 Setup script for deployment\n\nset -e\n\necho \"📦 Installing dependencies...\"\nsudo apt-get update\nsudo apt-get install -y docker.io docker-compose git curl\n\necho \"📥 Cloning repository...\"\ngit clone https://github.com/07Jhon/android-call-recording-agent.git\ncd android-call-recording-agent\n\necho \"🐳 Starting Docker services...\"\ndocker-compose up -d\n\necho \"✅ Services are running!\"\necho \"\"\necho \"🌐 Access URLs:\"\necho \"Backend API:    http://$(hostname -I | awk '{print $1}'):8080\"\necho \"Web Dashboard:  http://$(hostname -I | awk '{print $1}'):5173\"\necho \"Database GUI:   http://$(hostname -I | awk '{print $1}'):8081\"\necho \"\"\necho \"📝 Database Credentials:\"\necho \"Username: postgres\"\necho \"Password: postgres\"\necho \"Database: call_recordings\"\n", "path": "deploy/setup.sh"}, {"content": "# Deploy on Railway.app\n\n## 1. Create Railway Account\n- Go to https://railway.app\n- Sign in with GitHub\n\n## 2. Connect Repository\n- Click \"New Project\"\n- Select \"Deploy from GitHub\"\n- Choose your repository\n\n## 3. Configure Services\n- Add PostgreSQL service\n- Configure environment variables\n\n## 4. Deploy\n- Railway auto-deploys from main branch\n- Check deployment status in dashboard\n\n## Access\n- Backend: `https://your-project.railway.app`\n- Database: Railway provides connection string\n", "path": "deploy/RAILWAY.md"}, {"content": "runtime: java17\nenv: standard\nentrypoint: \"java -jar target/call-recording-backend-1.0.0.jar\"\n\nenv_variables:\n  SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL: \"${CLOUD_SQL_CONNECTION_NAME}\"\n  SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME: \"${DB_USER}\"\n  SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD: \"${DB_PASSWORD}\"\n", "path": "deploy/app.yaml"}, {"content": "{\n  \"name\": \"call-recording-backend\",\n  \"description\": \"Android Call Recording Backend API\",\n  \"repository\": \"https://github.com/07Jhon/android-call-recording-agent\",\n  \"keywords\": [\"call-recording\", \"java\", \"spring-boot\", \"postgresql\"],\n  \"buildpacks\": [\n    {\n      \"url\": \"heroku/java\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"addons\": [\n    {\n      \"plan\": \"heroku-postgresql:hobby-dev\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"env\": {\n    \"SPRING_JPA_HIBERNATE_DDL_AUTO\": {\n      \"description\": \"Hibernate DDL strategy\",\n      \"value\": \"validate\"\n    },\n    \"SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL\": {\n      \"description\": \"Database connection URL\",\n      \"value\": \"${DATABASE_URL}\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"formation\": {\n    \"web\": {\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"size\": \"free\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "path": "deploy/app.json"}, {"content": "# Render Deployment Guide\n\n## 1. Create Render Account\n- Go to https://render.com\n- Sign up with GitHub\n\n## 2. Create New Service\n- Click \"New +\" → \"Web Service\"\n- Connect GitHub repository\n- Select branch: main\n\n## 3. Configure\n- **Name**: call-recording-backend\n- **Environment**: Docker\n- **Build Command**: `docker-compose build`\n- **Start Command**: `docker-compose up`\n- **Region**: Choose closest to you\n\n## 4. Add Database\n- Click \"New +\" → \"PostgreSQL\"\n- Name: call-recording-db\n- Region: Same as service\n\n## 5. Environment Variables\n```\nSPRING_DATASOURCE_URL=postgresql://[USER]:[PASSWORD]@[HOST]:5432/call_recordings\nSPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME=[USER]\nSPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD=[PASSWORD]\n```\n\n## 6. Deploy\n- Click \"Create Web Service\"\n- Wait for deployment\n- Access your app at: `https://your-app.onrender.com`\n", "path": "deploy/RENDER.md"}, {"content": "# AWS Deployment Guide\n\n## Option 1: Elastic Beanstalk (Easiest)\n\n```bash\n# 1. Install EB CLI\npip install awsebcli\n\n# 2. Initialize\neb init -p java-17 call-recording-backend\n\n# 3. Create environment\neb create production\n\n# 4. Deploy\neb deploy\n\n# 5. Open app\neb open\n```\n\n## Option 2: RDS + EC2\n\n### Step 1: Create RDS PostgreSQL\n```bash\n# AWS Console → RDS → Create DB Instance\n# - Engine: PostgreSQL 15\n# - Instance class: db.t3.micro (free tier)\n# - Storage: 20 GB\n# - Public accessibility: Yes\n```\n\n### Step 2: Launch EC2 Instance\n```bash\n# AWS Console → EC2 → Instances → Launch\n# - AMI: Ubuntu 22.04 LTS\n# - Instance type: t3.micro (free tier)\n# - Security Group: Allow 8080, 5173\n```\n\n### Step 3: SSH and Setup\n```bash\nssh -i your-key.pem ubuntu@your-ec2-ip\n\n# Run setup script\nwget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/07Jhon/android-call-recording-agent/main/deploy/setup.sh\nchmod +x setup.sh\n./setup.sh\n```\n\n## Access\n- API: `http://your-ec2-ip:8080`\n- Dashboard: `http://your-ec2-ip:5173`\n- Database: RDS endpoint\n", "path": "deploy/AWS.md"}]